description:
Job Description
Under the overall supervision National Information Management and Database Officer – ACDMS and the direct supervision of the Senior Database and Software Developer Associate – ACDMS, and the technical supervision of the Database and Information Management Officer, the Database and Application Support Associate – ACDMS will be responsible for supporting the day-to-day operation, testing, maintenance, documentation and user support of the Afghanistan Centralised Database Management System (ACDMS). The incumbent will work closely with the ACDMS technical team, programme information management focal points, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and other relevant units, and will carry out assigned technical tasks in accordance with approved specifications, procedures and priorities.
ACDMS is a Country Office (CO)-wide institutional data management initiative intended to provide a centrally governed, secure, scalable and interoperable platform supporting beneficiary and service records, programme and project management, document management, referrals and case
management, needs and assessments, monitoring and evaluation, audit functions, reporting and analysis. The platform is intended to reduce fragmented systems and duplication while strengthening data quality, accountability, information security and evidence-informed decision-making.
The position provides hands-on application and database support within established technical frameworks. The incumbent will assist with routine application and configuration and updates, data validation and migration, software testing, incident resolution, reporting outputs, documentation and user assistance. System architecture, complex database design, enterprise integrations, technical approvals and release decisions remain the responsibility of the higher-level technical positions and established governance structures.
Responsibilities
Support the configuration, maintenance and routine enhancement of ACDMS applications and databases. Assist with updates to forms, fields, validation rules, reports and other system components in accordance with approved specifications and established procedures.
2. Support data import, migration, validation and quality-control activities. Conduct routine checks for completeness, consistency and accuracy of data, document findings and escalate unresolved issues as required.
3. Conduct assigned system testing activities, including functional, integration and user acceptance testing, in accordance with approved test cases and procedures. Assist with routine application and database maintenance, performance monitoring and implementation of approved system updates.
4. Provide first-line support to ACDMS users by responding to routine inquiries, assisting with user onboarding and training activities, and escalating complex or non-routine technical issues through established channels.
5.Assist in maintaining dashboards, reports, extracts and data-refresh processes. Verify outputs against approved definitions and report discrepancies or system issues.
6.Maintain technical documentation, user guides, issue logs, test records and configuration inventories. Follow approved version-control and change-management procedures.
7. Support user account administration and access management processes. Follow IOM data protection, information security, confidentiality and records-management requirements and report any suspected incidents or risks through established channels.
8. Work closely with the Senior Database and Developer Associate – ACDMS, National Information Management and Database Officer – ACDMS, Database and Information Management Officer, ICT colleagues and programme focal points to carry out assigned support tasks and contribute to the effective day-to-day operation of ACDMS.
9.Perform such other relevant duties as may be assigned.luding on-the-job training and mentorship.
10. Perform any other relevant duties as assigned by the supervisor.
Qualifications
Education
Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Information Systems, Software Development, Database Administration or a related field from an accredited academic institution with three years of relevant professional experience;
or
High School diploma with five years of relevant professional experience.
Experience
Experience providing application, database, data-management or information-technology support;
Experience using relational databases and SQL for routine queries, validation, reporting or data maintenance;
Experience supporting web-based applications or undertaking basic development, scripting or configuration tasks;
Experience conducting software testing, documenting defects and verifying corrections;
Experience cleaning, mapping, importing, validating or reconciling data;
Experience providing user support, recording incidents and escalating complex technical issues;
Experience maintaining technical documentation, user guidance, issue logs or configuration records;
Experience with version-control, ticketing or change-management tools is an advantage; and,
Experience with reporting, dashboards or business-intelligence tools is an advantage.
Skills:
Working knowledge of relational database concepts and SQL;
Basic knowledge of web applications, programming or scripting and the ability to work within established development frameworks;
Ability to perform structured data cleaning, validation, import and reconciliation tasks accurately;
Ability to execute test cases, reproduce problems and document clear technical findings;
Good troubleshooting and user-support skills, including appropriate escalation of complex or sensitive issues;
Familiarity with version control, issue tracking, reporting tools or application-support workflows is an advantage;
Awareness of data protection, confidentiality, access control and information-security principles;
Good organisational, documentation and communication skills; and,
Ability to follow technical instructions, manage assigned tasks and work collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team.
Required Skills
Job info
Contract Type: Special Short Term Graded (Up to 9 months)
Initial Contract Duration: Based on funding availability
Org Type: Country Office
Vacancy Type: Special Vacancy Notice
Recruiting Type: General Service
Grade: G-5
Is this S/VN based in an L3 office or in support to an L3 emergency response?: No

Quem somos?
Somos a Fuerza Studio , uma empresa fundada em 2010, especializada em global web, design e branding. Com uma atuação internacional, já entregamos projetos em mais de 20 países e estamos envolvidos em cerca de 40 projetos ativos, a maioria com foco global.
Nosso time é composto por cerca de 40 colaboradores, organizados em equipes multidisciplinares e colaborativas. Acreditamos em um ambiente saudável, humano e de constante aprendizado — e é isso que nos move há mais de uma década.
O que oferecemos?
Descanso Remunerado: 2 dias úteis por mês, a partir do segundo mês (22 dias úteis no ciclo de 12 meses).
Day-Off: No dia do seu aniversário e em feriados nacionais.
Inglês: Aulas de conversação em grupo.
Educação contínua: Acesso à Alura + apoio para cursos e certificações.
Qual o perfil da vaga?
Estamos procurando um(a) Desenvolvedor(a) Backend Pleno com domínio em Go, apaixonado por criar soluções escaláveis, bem estruturadas e com atenção à performance. Buscamos alguém que tenha bagagem técnica, mas também vontade de apoiar o crescimento técnico do time.
Essa posição exige interação com clientes não brasileiros, então proficiência em inglês é fundamental.
Requisitos Obrigatórios:
4+ anos de experiência em desenvolvimento backend;
Domínio em Go (Golang);
Experiência em Typescript;
Experiência com arquitetura de sistemas distribuídos;
Prática com APIs RESTful e GraphQL;
Experiência com AWS (Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB);
Experiência com IaC (Terraform);
Experiência com microsserviços;
Experiência com GIT e metodologias ágeis (Scrum/Kanban)
Diferenciais:
Noções de CI/CD e observabilidade (monitoramento/logs);
Certificações em AWS;
Conhecimento em containers (Docker/Kubernetes);
Participação ativa em comunidades de tecnologia ou projetos open source.
